## Approach

Alien `i` becomes an adult at time `i`. At that moment, each adult `k < i` with at least one stone gives it one stone. Let `S_i = A_i + G_i`, where `G_i` is the number of gifts alien `i` receives. Alien `k` donates at every event `i > k` until its stones run out, so it donates at times `k+1 .. min(k+S_k, N)`. Therefore:

- `G_i` = number of donors `k < i` whose donation window covers `i`.
- Alien `i` gives away `min(S_i, N-i)` stones, so `B_i = max(0, S_i - (N-i))`.

A difference array tracks the donation windows, so the whole computation is O(N). I checked the recurrence against sample 1 (output `2 0 10 5`) and hand-simulated each test case below.

